                        ],
                        "form": "die Ganser"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69ce6a62-01a0-313b-8de5-d10f1b350bea",
                        "entry_id": "5d4abef4-7f59-3b03-92ac-fba4cd87ba4a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "männliche Gans"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Austrian German",
                            "South-German"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72b52a6a-51c3-4a3b-81c8-0ec4ccb173e8",
                                "sense_id": "69ce6a62-01a0-313b-8de5-d10f1b350bea",
                                "text": "Das Männchen heißt Ganser und das Weibchen Gans; der Ganser hat längere Füße als die Gans und eine sehr laute Stimme. (1812)"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0047fec-34d8-4a23-80bc-7062acc4f034",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d4abef4-7f59-3b03-92ac-fba4cd87ba4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "69ce6a62-01a0-313b-8de5-d10f1b350bea",
                        "source_sense_description": "österreichisch, süddeutsch: männliche Gans",
                        "target_lang_word": "gander",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gander",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07f147cc-5e7f-3d9c-9d07-004bdb8c389b",
                                        "entry_id": "058b2146-8213-3f81-9997-e95cea4b6aae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male goose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6387c073-142d-471b-a218-3ed690567c1a",
                                                "sense_id": "07f147cc-5e7f-3d9c-9d07-004bdb8c389b",
                                                "text": "Ganders and geese are at their best for stock from two to ten years old. They live to a great age—it is stated to thirty or more years—but after ten years they cannot be reckoned upon as reliable assets on a farm. Two years old is the best age to mate them, making up pens of a gander and two or three geese at the New Year. It is difficult sometimes to distinguish ganders from geese. A practical man is, however, rarely mistaken."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54a3be7f-3380-4432-8899-15cff97c24e3",
                                                "sense_id": "07f147cc-5e7f-3d9c-9d07-004bdb8c389b",
                                                "text": "Old Mother Goose / When she wanted to wander / Would ride through the air / On a very fine gander."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44f8af48-c507-4b69-be23-41e6525b003f",
                                                "sense_id": "07f147cc-5e7f-3d9c-9d07-004bdb8c389b",
                                                "text": "Marta's gander was a magnificent snow-white bird: the object of terror to foxes, children and dogs. She had reared him as a gosling; and whenever he approached, he would let fly a low contented burble and sidle his neck around her thighs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a24d0c4d-857a-3e79-aefc-dc6450bab6ca",
                                        "entry_id": "058b2146-8213-3f81-9997-e95cea4b6aae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fool, simpleton."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38440484-4c09-34fc-aae9-cdd895242fe6",
                                        "entry_id": "058b2146-8213-3f81-9997-e95cea4b6aae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A glance, look."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ed566da-52a5-4037-afe7-43404ee819cc",
                                                "sense_id": "38440484-4c09-34fc-aae9-cdd895242fe6",
                                                "text": "Have a gander at what he’s written."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c58f883c-0e62-41e9-970d-6f7ef76de9bd",
                                                "sense_id": "38440484-4c09-34fc-aae9-cdd895242fe6",
                                                "text": "I took a gander and she seemed so familiar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1df8337-e227-4851-a232-f72f69e45dce",
                                                "sense_id": "38440484-4c09-34fc-aae9-cdd895242fe6",
                                                "text": "As well as the church and its sexton, the market house is worth a gander, while the hop fields and orchards are \"reminding one of Kent\", for we are in another \"Garden of England\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dc4ed37-c3a2-375e-b01d-1cacf561e7b9",
                                        "entry_id": "058b2146-8213-3f81-9997-e95cea4b6aae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man living apart from his wife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gander",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95a84ad1-b01d-3406-a851-dfe623bd400f",
                                        "entry_id": "a841ec30-ebd4-3668-90b3-211e9909285f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to ramble, wander"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bba3bf74-bd85-4cdd-aec2-6c98aaae7208",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d4abef4-7f59-3b03-92ac-fba4cd87ba4a",
                        "source_sense_id": "69ce6a62-01a0-313b-8de5-d10f1b350bea",
                        "source_sense_description": "österreichisch, süddeutsch: männliche Gans",
                        "target_lang_word": "gąsior",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gąsior",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf8e4b10-530f-370b-b3cc-551f20df0ff5",
                                        "entry_id": "07c32ab2-a3e0-351c-8394-9f61ecf28618",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "samiec gęsi"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed47d720-b95d-499a-be93-f29101f5cb39",
                                                "sense_id": "cf8e4b10-530f-370b-b3cc-551f20df0ff5",
                                                "text": "Wzbija się kurzawa na piaszczystej drodze, wrzask gęsi miesza się z pokrzykiwaniem pastuszków, klaskanie biczów rozlega się szeroko w powietrzu, a nad całym tym gwarem panuje przeraźliwy krzyk sołtysowego gąsiora, który idzie, machając skrzydłami, przed stadem jakby wódz przed wojskiem."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gąsior",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89b323e4-0581-3ef7-a93d-e6487f301f4e",
                                        "entry_id": "8a59919d-a696-35d2-bef0-20bcf573ee07",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "pękate naczynie szklane z wąską szyjką służące do przechowywania płynów oraz do produkcji win lub nalewek"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a8f7262-2b33-46ac-80af-51df03576e02",
                                                "sense_id": "89b323e4-0581-3ef7-a93d-e6487f301f4e",
                                                "text": "Zupełnie szpetne były pudła i pudełka, które ściśle przy sobie na półkach stojąc, okrywały ściany pstrokacizną barw wyblakłych lub zaśniedziałych, lecz przewyższały je w szpetności butle, butelki, gąsiory i słoje, płynami kolorów nijakich napełnione, a okrywające stoły, na których jeszcze więdły cytryny, gniły jabłka, czerstwiały bułki i spaloną żółtością od pstrego tła odznaczały się aż ku brudnej podłodze zwieszające się wieńce obwarzanków."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2.1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "004b4df8-8b1f-3aa6-92f0-97dd833df5df",
